       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the clinical rationale. No indication I know of supports metformin at 5,100 mg/day, and doses that high carry a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. A single 1,700 mg dose is also double the usual maximum per dose. Your confirmation doesn't change that risk for the patient.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter the maximum labeled dose now.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). You or the team can then adjust it if needed.\n- **Get a pharmacist or attending review.** If you think a dose above the labeled maximum is warranted, pharmacy or the attending can review it and enter it through your institution's process for exceptions. That process usually includes documenting the rationale and setting up monitoring.\n- **Enter a different regimen.** Tell me the dose and frequency, and I'll enter it.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order?"
      }
